vironment that can integrate into an existing electronic health record system or stand-alone if no electronic health record (EHR) is present. It also offers jSign, an electronic and digital signature solution; eFax Conductor, an interface engine and interoperability platform that provides integration technology; eFax Clarity that transforms unstructured documents into structured actionable data; and eFax, an online faxing solution, as well as other products under the MyFax, Sfax, MetroFax, and SRfax brands. In addition, the company offers Clarity Clinical Documentation (CD), a clinical documentation software; eFax Harmony, an API for healthcare; eFax All Access for care coordination; and artificial intelligence, clinical documentation, HIPAA compliance, natural language processing, interoperability, eSignatures, and cloud fax solutions. It serves individuals and small businesses; and the healthcare, government, financial services, law, education, insurance, manufacturing, and real estate sectors. Consensus Cloud Solutions, Inc. was incorporated in 2021 and is headquartered in Los Angeles, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. R. Scott Turicchi | CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 520 people. Revenue per employee of $672K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $204K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $34K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Consensus Cloud Solutions, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $687M market cap on $350M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 81% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $106M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.61\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Goodwill represents 53% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.7pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 54/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 15% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 36% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 67% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 56% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Does Consensus Cloud Solutions (CCSI) Have the Potential to Rally 28.44% as Wall Street Analysts Expect?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3033134/does-consensus-cloud-solutions-ccsi-have-the-potential-to-rally-28-44-as-wall-street-analysts-expect?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cconsensus_price_target-3033134","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795182904.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (CCSI)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_CCSI_112026083001_1795181401.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795181401.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Consensus Cloud Solutions (CCSI) Upgraded to Buy: Here's Why","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3031969/consensus-cloud-solutions-ccsi-upgraded-to-buy-here-s-why?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3031969","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795017603.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","analyst_a